#   outdir dv/auto_dv/out_t11w/build/gen_tb (the build carries the fix).
# Run: gen_ut_intg_span with +gen_ut_intg_span_arm_count=1 (the B16 case), seed 1,
#   dv/auto_dv/out_t11w/runs/b16_c1/waves.fsdb, one collected UVM_ERROR and its id is isa_rd.
# Read with the fsdb-mcp-server against dv/auto_dv/out_t11w/build/gen_tb/vcs_simv.daidir. Times are the FSDB's
# own 10 ps unit; the TB clock period is 10 ns, so one cycle is 1000.
# crash_dump_o is {current_pc, next_pc, last_data_addr, exception_pc, exception_addr}.
# gen_span_buf = 0x800002e0; the load is lw a1, 2(a0), effective address 0x800002e2, spanning the words at
# 0x800002e0 and 0x800002e4, and the ONE armed corruption hits the first of them.

data_addr_o     42500 = 800002e0   46500 = 800002e4     (the two accesses of the misaligned load)
data_rvalid_i   49000 -> 1  50000 -> 0   54000 -> 1  55000 -> 0   (the two response beats)
crash_dump_o    46500 = {80000118, 8000011c, 800002e2, 00000000, 00000000}
                50500 = {80000118, 8000011c, 800002e4, 00000000, 00000000}
                55500 = {80000118, 8000027c, 800002e4, 8000011c, 800002e2}
                63500 = {8000027c, 80000280, 800002e4, 8000011c, 800002e2}
                ... exception_addr holds 800002e2 through every following record in the window
rvfi_ext_rf_wr_suppress  no transition in 400..900 ns: the flag stays CLEAR, which is bug candidate B16

## What the window shows, and why the correction cannot sit inside the suppress-flag block
At 55500, one cycle after the second response, the DUT latches its exception mirror: exception_pc is the
load's own pc 0x8000011c and EXCEPTION_ADDR IS 0x800002E2, the access address, not the announced word address
0x800002e0. That matches rtl/ibex_controller.sv:416 with rtl/ibex_load_store_unit.sv:258: the internal NMI's
mtval is the LSU's last address, and for a misaligned access whose FIRST word carried the corruption that is
the access address. And rvfi_ext_rf_wr_suppress never rises in the window, so the record the scoreboard sees
has the flag clear. The correction that turns the announced word address into the access address therefore
has to run for this record, and before this fix it ran only inside the block guarded by that flag, so the
model kept 0x800002e0 and the crash_dump rule fired once per following record until the window drained.
